      "properties": {
        "snippet": "Represents recreation sites so small they are displayed as points Recreation sites are grouped hierarchically. For example, a campground may be composed of many loops, which may be composed of many campsites. The campground may also include other facilities such as boating areas and picnic grounds. Campgrounds may be grouped into complexes. There are four levels to this hierarchy but not all levels are necessarily used for any given site and some recreation subtypes may occur at more than one level of the hierarchy, depending on which other recreation sites they are associated with on the ground. Although this hierarchy is not described in the GIS Core Data, it is described in the associated INFRA ORACLE tables. Associated National Application: INFRA Recreation",
